From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-fix <build@ci>
Date: Fri, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] include/linux/log2.h: fix noreturn+const attribute conflict (GCC 11)

GCC 11 introduced a warning (upgraded to error by -Werror) when a
function declaration carries both __attribute__((const)) and
__attribute__((noreturn)), because "const" implies the function returns
a value, while "noreturn" means it never returns — the two are
contradictory.

The noreturn attribute on ____ilog2_NaN() was originally added to
produce a link-time error when ilog2() is called with a constant 0 or
non-power-of-2 argument. The const attribute already makes the compiler
treat it as a pure function and handles constant folding. Removing
noreturn silences the GCC 11 -Werror=attributes diagnostic while
preserving all existing functionality.

This matches the fix applied in the upstream Linux kernel:
  commit 53bf7963ae76 ("include/linux/log2.h: remove noreturn from
  __ilog2_NaN")

Fixes: board/sunxi/board.c compilation failure:
  include/linux/log2.h:26:1: error: ignoring attribute 'noreturn'
  because it conflicts with attribute 'const' [-Werror=attributes]
---
 include/linux/log2.h | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/log2.h b/include/linux/log2.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/include/linux/log2.h
+++ b/include/linux/log2.h
@@ -20,8 +20,7 @@
  * deal with unrepresentable constant logarithms
  */
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM
-extern __attribute__((const, noreturn))
+extern __attribute__((const))
 #endif
 
 int ____ilog2_NaN(void);
